z0z|v|To form an opinion concerning, without knowledge or means of knowledge; to judge of at random; to conjecture. ; To judge or form an opinion of, from reasons that seem preponderating, but are not decisive. ; To solve by a correct conjecture; to conjecture rightly; as, he who guesses the riddle shall have the ring; he has guessed my designs. ; To hit upon or reproduce by memory. ; To think; to suppose; to believe; to imagine; -- followed by an objective clause. ; To make a guess or random judgment; to conjecture; -- with at, about, etc.	d:1tvt,8,6~1tvt,8,6
