z6a|n|A narrow passage of water; as, the Gut of Canso. ; An intenstine; a bowel; the whole alimentary canal; the enteron; (pl.) bowels; entrails. ; One of the prepared entrails of an animal, esp. of a sheep, used for various purposes. See Catgut. ; The sac of silk taken from a silkworm (when ready to spin its cocoon), for the purpose of drawing it out into a thread. This, when dry, is exceedingly strong, and is used as the snood of a fish line.	a:1mx1,27,4~1mx1,27,4	V:280r,68,10;trs,43,3;1ybo,11,1;trq,2,1~280r,68,10;trs,43,3;trq,2,1;1ybo,11,1	N:15i3,81,2;trs,47,4;280r,45,2~trs,47,4;15i3,81,2;280r,45,2
